      <activity id="c1f6ed42-76e9-595d-bbc4-f6cf3f6707cf" activityNameId="7f5fe81c-26ec-5a39-9013-e5a439851963" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, high voltage, supply mix GO, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, high voltage, supply mix GO, at grid
This dataset describes the transmission of high voltage electricity.; UUID:ecce65a4-87b1-355d-9f3b-e754605c3887
Included are the electricity production in Switzerland and from imports, the transmission network and direct emissions to air (ozone and N2O). Electricity losses are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Ozone- and NO2-emission factors are based on published measurements made in various countries.  Transmission network, losses and emissions are taken from Itten, Frischknecht and Stucki (2014): LCI of Electricity Mixes and Grid.
Technology: Average technology used to transmit and distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistical data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ecce65a4-87b1-355d-9f3b-e754605c3887.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
